SHAMSU — the framed TUI: output pane, sidebar, pinned input, own scrollback
===========================================================================
2026-08-22 · branch small-shamsu-new

Spec item 01 in full ("a real layout instead of a scrolling log") and item 02
(the right sidebar). The earlier pass delivered item 01's LISTED requirements -
pinned box, echo, backspace, history, output above - but not its headline, and
put the telemetry on two bottom rows instead of in a pane. This is the frame.


THE OBJECTION, AND WHY IT DOES NOT SURVIVE
------------------------------------------
I argued a frame costs the terminal's own scrollback. True, and not a reason:
Neovim and lazygit take the alternate screen and implement scrolling INSIDE the
application. `LogPane` is that scrollback - bounded, wrapped, scrollable with
the wheel, PageUp/PageDown and Ctrl+Home/End - and it does not move when the
sidebar or the input box repaint.


